  "term": "CRH",
  "definition": "CRH refers to corticotropin-releasing hormone or factor, a stress-related signaling molecule active in brain regions such as the amygdala and hypothalamus. In this psychology-related biological context, it is discussed because changes in its signaling may contribute to fear, anxiety, depression, pain, and responses to stress or trauma.",
